  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 146 PM CDT Mon Jun 22 2026\n\nThe upper-level ridge looks to remain centered over far west Texas \nthrough at least Thursday. A rinse-and-repeat pattern of hot \ntemperatures with breezy southerly winds each day will continue for \nWednesday and Thursday as the \"heat dome\" persists.  At this point, \nheat indices look to stay below 104 degrees but this will be \nreevaluated each day for additional heat advisories. Rain chances\nappear to be next to nothing, aside from any late-evening \nthunderstorms that occur due to weaknesses in the ridge. Late \nThursday through Friday and Saturday, models show broad upper- \nlevel troughing will develop over the western US and flatten out \nthe ridge across Texas. While some chances for rain showers and \nthunderstorms could be introduced, this will likely take place \nacross the higher terrain of west Texas and be very localized. \nOtherwise, the hot pattern should continue with near to above- \nnormal temperatures. In fact parts parts of the Big Country could \nreach highs above 106 for this weekend. Currently there is a low \nto medium (20-50%) chance of this occurring.",
